\": \"highest median silhouette across seeds\",\n    \"tie_breaker\": \"highest mean_pairwise_ari\",\n    \"selected_resolution\": 0.4\n  },\n  \"n_clusters\": 6,\n  \"cluster_size_summary\": {\n    \"minimum_cells\": 55,\n    \"minimum_cluster\": \"0\",\n    \"maximum_cells\": 2002,\n    \"maximum_cluster\": \"4\"\n  },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"silhouette\": 0.09877394884824753,\n    \"calinski_harabasz\": 399.0818721500154,\n    \"davies_bouldin\": 2.099185446658115,\n    \"metric_cells\": 3000,\n    \"mean_pairwise_ari\": 0.7593371237165119,\n    \"min_pairwise_ari\": 0.5980176805106856,\n    \"mean_pairwise_nmi\": 0.7503357188109883,\n    \"min_pairwise_nmi\": 0.6157218171960022,\n    \"median_silhouette\": 0.11710669100284576\n  },\n  \"matched_kmeans_control_metrics\": {\n    \"silhouette\": 0.09451214969158173,\n    \"calinski_harabasz\": 417.1874767972408,\n    \"davies_bouldin\": 2.1559270251297376,\n    \"metric_cells\": 3000\n  },\n  \"baseline_silhouette_summary\": {\n    \"HVG\": 0.1676386147737503,\n    \"random_min\": 0.09164907783269882,\n    \"random_max\": 0.1314728856086731,\n    \"random_mean\": 0.10683469435102061\n  },\n  \"random_control_comparison\": {\n    \"metabolic_matched_kmeans_silhouette\": 0.09451214969158173,\n    \"random_controls_exceeding_or_equal\": 17,\n    \"random_controls_total\": 19,\n    \"add_one_rank_fraction\": 0.9,\n    \"interpretation\": \"descriptive add-one rank, not the observed exceedance proportion and not a biological P value\"\n  },\n  \"categorical_confounder_nmi\": {\n    \"patient\": 0.3934021350739383,\n    \"sample\": 0.4429005416166666,\n    \"source\": 0.3473174298703783,\n    \"cell_cycle_phase\": 0.27380724445207655\n  },\n  \"cell_type_association_summary\": {},\n  \"within_replicate_summary\": {\n    \"replicate_field\": \"patient\",\n    \"replicates_analyzed\": 3,\n    \"global_vs_within_ari_min\": 0.511314622242799,\n    \"global_vs_within_ari_max\": 0.8446121500396181,\n    \"weakest_replicate\": \"6\",\n    \"weakest_replicate_cells\": 2776\n  },\n  \"evidence_checks\": {\n    \"stable_mean_ari_at_least_0_75\": true,\n    \"positive_descriptive_silhouette\": true,\n    \"higher_matched_k_silhouette_than_all_random_gene_controls\": false,\n    \"all_clusters_supported_by_at_least_two_replicates\": false,\n    \"not_dominated_by_patient_sample_or_cell_type_nmi_at_least_0_5\": true,\n    \"random_baseline_exceedance_fraction_not_a_biological_p_value\": 0.9\n  },\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Silhouette is estimated on a fixed random subset; all QC-passing cells are retained for PCA, graph construction, and clustering.\",\n    \"The unsupervised question has no predefined condition contrast; no cell-level differential-expression P values are reported.\",\n    \"No significance test is performed on data-derived cluster labels; within-replicate reclustering is descriptive and not held-out donor validation.\",\n    \"Random gene controls are matched in size, not expression mean or dispersion; their exceedance fraction is a descriptive benchmark, not a biological P value.\",\n    \"Resolution was selected using the same dataset. ARI/NMI assess Leiden randomization conditional on the fixed PCA/neighbor graph, not all preprocessing uncertainty.\",\n    \"A threshold on confounder NMI does not establish independence; independent validation, QC/batch sensitivity and a continuum-versus-discrete comparison remain necessary.\",\n    \"Identical source gene symbols are summed before QC/normalization. Symbol-level aggregation preserves library counts but does not disambiguate stable gene IDs or distinct loci.\",\n    \"Gene symbols are matched exactly first and then by unique case-insensitive equivalence. The saved mapping, unmatched symbols and ambiguities must be reviewed before biological interpretation.\"\n  ]\n}\n"},{"key":"read_file:2ea4520399a21b5f4b1dfa91d70aa274aeb5a9aff7ce74e54f4cb280574e5ad1:56","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8fba063c5f0ff56","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T17:20:49.919Z","result":"\n\\section{Results}\n\n\\subsection{Question 1: Global Metabolic Grouping Reproducibility}\n\nUsing the user-supplied metabolic gene set on all 58,843 cells, we identified 17 clusters at resolution 0.8. The clustering shows descriptive associations with cell type (NMI = 0.496) and cell subtype (NMI = 0.648), indicating that metabolic gene expression patterns are strongly influenced by cell identity.\n\n\\begin{figure}[h!]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/metabolic_umap.pdf}\n\\caption{UMAP visualization of all cells colored by metabolic gene-derived clusters (17 clusters). Each point represents a cell, colored according to its cluster assignment from Leiden clustering on the metabolic gene set.}\n\\label{fig:metabolic_umap}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\begin{figure}[h!]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/clustering_diagnostics.pdf}\n\\caption{Clustering diagnostics for global metabolic gene analysis. Panel (a) shows silhouette scores across resolution values; panel (b) displays pairwise ARI stability across random seeds. The selected resolution (0.8) maximizes median silhouette score (0.222) while maintaining stability (mean pairwise ARI = 0.965).}\n\\label{fig:global_diagnostics}\n\\end{figure}\n"},{"key":"read_file:7483d5702fbf8d7e6b20b466237fc4f3708f7b687b86cc882a011a2ed0a977ab:56","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7e856ab38a4e22c","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T17:20:26.592Z","result":"ERROR: ENOENT: no such file or directory, lstat 'C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\3CA\\QA_R4\\results\\core_analysis\\summary.json'"},{"key":"read_file:3065bf4cf82d86503134b8d7b965b6a2430284840feb46eabcfe54e5c5c78461:56","