l-type association:} The clustering shows strong association with cell type (NMI = 0.942) and cell subtype (NMI = 0.938). Stratified analysis by cell type shows that within each cell type, the metabolic clustering is dominated by cell type identity rather than independent metabolic states.\n\n\\textbf{Patient/sample confounding:} Patient NMI = 0.187, Sample NMI = 0.203. The clustering is not dominated by patient or sample factors (both NMI < 0.5).\n\n\\textbf{Within-replicate sensitivity:} Across 3 patients, the global ARI ranges from 0.511 to 0.845, with patient 6 being the weakest replicate (2,776 cells).\n\n\\begin{figure}[h!]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/metabolic_umap.pdf}\n\\caption{UMAP embedding of 58,843 cells colored by metabolic clustering (17 clusters) using 1,646 metabolic genes. Cells are nested within patients and samples.}\n\\label{fig:global_umap}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\begin{figure}[h!]\n\\centering"},{"key":"read_file:d15a8b057fc1c0658f9f1ff598984a0782e57143541113da93f7a64d233d114d:66","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9273fbc061ecee2","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T17:47:49.875Z","result":"{\n  \"engine\": \"workflow_research_quality_metabolic_states_v2\",\n  \"engine_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\Desktop\\\\agentic\\\\workflow_codex\\\\tools\\\\research-quality\\\\metabolic_states.py\",\n  \"engine_sha256\": \"51ddbf26c336a932f10d216db6092bc5aa24f402adf9dafee6a0435382592401\",\n  \"methods\": {\n    \"unit\": \"Exact-symbol aggregated raw counts; all source features form each cell library-size denominator\",\n    \"normalization\": \"Per-cell library size to 10000, then log1p\",\n    \"feature_scaling\": \"Scanpy scale(zero_center=False, max_value=10)\",\n    \"pca\": {\n      \"solver\": \"arpack\",\n      \"zero_center\": true,\n      \"components\": 30,\n      \"seed\": 0\n 