ntation\": \"genes_by_cells\",\n    \"cell_id_column\": \"cell_name\"\n  },\n  \"feature_set\": {\n    \"name\": \"User-supplied metabolic genes\",\n    \"source_url\": \"local-user-supplied-input\",\n    \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-13T15:15:45.001Z\",\n    \"sha256\": \"7503180d29693bd1e654ea93281db0e3ec4177ff44842c8b02f6a098402e41a9\",\n    \"genes_path\": \"inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv\",\n    \"matched_genes_path\": \"results/core_analysis/matched_metabolic_genes.txt\",\n    \"source_gene_count\": 1988,\n    \"matched_gene_count\": 1646\n  },\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"engine\": \"workflow_research_quality_metabolic_states_v2\",\n    \"core_result_path\": \"results/core_analysis/core_result.json\",\n    \"core_result_sha256\": \"0da19b546073463f6341cb411b21287f3e50b2b9733a6f39dfc53e1fb9ca5848\",\n    \"input_unit\": \"cell\",\n    \"rows_analyzed\": 58843,\n    \"unique_cells_analyzed\": 58843,\n    \"random_seeds\": [0],\n    \"baselines\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"HVG and random size-matched controls\",\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"random_controls_exceeding_or_equal\": 2,\n          \"random_controls_total\": 19,\n          \"add_one_rank_fraction\": 0.15\n        },\n        \"result_path\": \"results/core_analysis/baseline_metrics.csv\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"confounders_checked\": [\"patient\", \"cell_type\", \"sample\", \"source\", \"cell_subtype\", \"cell_cycle_phase\", \"complexity\", \"computed_total_counts\", \"computed_detected_genes\", \"computed_mito_percent\"],\n    \"methods\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Scanpy Leiden on supplied metabolic genes\",\n        \"labels_path\": \"results/core_analysis/cluster_labels.csv\",\n        \"cell_id_column\": \"cell_name\",\n        \"label_column\": \"cluster\",\n        \"n_clusters\": 17,\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"silhouette\": 0.21661581099033356,\n          \"mean_pairwise_ari\": 0.9650730581380069,\n          \"median_silhouette\": 0.22155894339084625\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"subgroup_analyses\": [\n      {\n        \"scope\": {\n          \"field\": \"cell_subtype\",\n          \"values\": [\"CD8 T cells\"]\n        },\n        \"core_result_path\": \"results/cd8_analysis/core_result.json\",\n        \"core_result_sha256\": \"50950f343600c9c0dd17ed5191a3511cc2fb397d1b026120f4fe47ca6ab1f102\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"references\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"choudhury_2022\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8\",\n      \"metadata_path\": \"sources/literature/crossref_db798362115f799a.json\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"artifacts\": {\n    \"tex\": \"report/main.tex\",\n    \"pdf\": \"report/main.pdf\",\n    \"summary\": \"results/summary.json\",\n    \"figures\": [\n      \"figures/metabolic_umap.pdf\",\n      \"figures/clustering_diagnostics.pdf\",\n      \"figures/cd8_analysis/metabolic_umap.pdf\",\n      \"figures/cd8_analysis/clustering_diagnostics.pdf\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n"},{"key":"read_file:7d6441497d2a000b8143602a7817c90abe7db88e139f89c062a1c36cfe0ad9d6:83","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b0442f1ee8df433","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T18:40:26.784Z","result":"# QA_R4: Metabolic State Analysis of Meningioma Single-Cell Data\n\n## Overview\n\nThis repository contains the analysis of transcriptional metabolic states using user-supplied metabolic genes on the Choudhury et al. 2022 brain single-cell RNA-seq dataset (3CA:20773).\n\n## Dataset\n\n- **Study**: Choudhury et al. 2022 - \"Meningioma DNA methylation groups identify biological drivers and therapeutic vulnerabilities\"\n- **3CA ID**: 3ca:20773\n- **DOI**: 10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8\n- **Technology**: 10x Genomics\n- **Samples**: 10\n- **Total cells**: 58,843\n\n## Data Sources\n\n### 3CA Raw Count Data\n- **Archive**: Data_Choudhury2022_Brain.tar.gz\n- **SHA-256**: 2156a73fd5f95a198ef90821f2d734bfa7e0b5aa3686deefd1b5c5d5d1269aa1\n- **Expression matrix**: inputs/Exp_data_UMIcounts.mtx (33,538 genes × 58,843 cells)\n- **Cells metadata**: inputs/Cells.csv\n- **Genes list**: inputs/Genes.txt\n\n### User-Supplied Metabolic Genes\n- **File**: inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv\n- **SHA-256**: 7503180d29693bd1e654ea93281db0e3ec4177ff44842c8b02f6a098402e41a9\n- **Source gene count**: 1,988 symbols\n- **Matched genes after prevalence filtering**: 1,646 (global analysis), 1,318 (CD8 T cells subset)\n\n## Analysis Results\n\n### Question 1: Metabolic State Clustering (All Cells)\n\n**Analysis scope**: 58,843 cells using 1,646 metabolic genes\n\n**Clustering results**:\n- **Number of clusters**: 17\n- **Selected resolution**: 0.8 (highest median silhouette across stable candidates)\n- **Cluster size range**: 714 - 8,806 cells\n\n**Metrics**:\n- Silhouette: 0.217\n- Calinski-Harabasz: 6,731\n- Davies-Bouldin: 1.58\n- Mean pairwise ARI: 0.965\n- Mean pairwise NMI: 0.968\n\n**Control comparisons**:\n- HVG silhouette: 0.283 (stronger than metabolic features)\n- Random control silhouette range: 0.20 - 0.22\n- Metabolic-matched KMeans silhouette: 0.220\n- Random controls exceeding or equal: 2 of 19 (add-one rank fraction: 0.15)\n\n**Confounder analysis**:\n- Patient NMI: 0.518\n- Sample NMI: 0.548\n- Cell type NMI: 0.496\n- Cell subtype NMI: 0.648\n\n**Conclusion**: Inconclusive. The analysis describes cell-group separation using metabolic genes but does not establish discrete biological metabolic states. The HVG baseline shows stronger clustering than metabolic features. Random controls show similar silhouette values, and the random control exceedance fraction (0.15) is a descriptive benchmark, not a biological P value.\n\n### Question 2: Cell Type Association\n\n**Global cell-type association**:\n- Cell type global NMI: 0.496\n- Within-replicate NMI range: 0.379 - 0.745 (median: 0.592)\n- Replicates assessable: 6\n\n**Cell subtype association**:\n- Cell subtype global NMI: 0.648\n- Within-replicate NMI range: 0.224 - 0.680 (median: 0.636)\n- Replicates assessable: 6\n\n**Within-replicate sensitivity**:\n- Replicates analyzed: 6\n- Global vs within ARI range: 0.071 - 0.676\n- Weakest replicate: 3 (3,287 cells)\n\n**Interpretation**: Cell type and cell subtype show moderate association with metabolic clusters (NMI ~0.5-0.65). The within-replicate \n...[OUTPUT TRUNCATED: kept first 3000 and last 3000 of 8052 characters; use filters or save output to a workspace file]...\nity**: The within-replicate NMI varies substantially, with some replicates showing weaker associations. This limits the ability to claim robust metabolic state separation.\n\n4. **Random control comparison**: The random control exceedance fraction is a descriptive benchmark, not a biological P value. In the global analysis, 2 of 19 random controls exceeded the metabolic features (0.15 add-one rank fraction). In the CD8 analysis, 17 of 19 exceeded (0.9 add-one rank fraction).\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **Descriptive only**: All metrics are descriptive; no significance tests are performed on data-derived cluster labels.\n- **No independent validation**: Within-replicate reclustering is not held-out donor validation.\n- **Confounder sensitivity**: Patient and sample NMI values indicate potential confounding by these factors.\n- **Continuum vs discrete**: The analysis does not test whether metabolic states are discrete or continuous.\n- **Symbol-level aggregation**: Identical source gene symbols are summed before QC/normalization, which preserves library counts but does not disambiguate stable gene IDs.\n\n## Files\n\n- `report/main.tex` - LaTeX report\n- `report/main.pdf` - Compiled PDF report\n- `results/summary.json` - Global analysis summary\n- `results/analysis_manifest.json` - Analysis manifest with all metadata\n- `results/core_analysis/core_result.json` - Global core analysis results\n- `results/core_analysis/cluster_labels.csv` - Global cluster labels\n- `results/core_analysis/matched_metabolic