 ranged from 0.071 to 0.676, with patient 3 being the weakest replicate (3,287 cells).\n\n\\subsubsection{Figure 1: Global UMAP}\n\\begin{figure}[h!]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/metabolic_umap.pdf}\n\\caption{UMAP embedding of all 58,843 cells colored by metabolic cluster (17 clusters) at resolution 0.8. Cells are colored by cluster label, with cluster sizes ranging from 714 to 8,806 cells.}\n\\label{fig:global_umap}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\subsubsection{Figure 2: Global Clustering Diagnostics}\n\\begin{figure}[h!]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/clustering_diagnostics.pdf}\n\\caption{Clustering diagnostics for global metabolic state analysis. Panel (a) shows silhouette scores across seeds; panel (b) shows pairwise ARI; panel (c) shows cluster size distribution.}\n\\label{fig:global_diagnostics}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\subsection{Question 2: Cell-Type Association}\n\\subsubsection{Association Summary}\nThe cell\\_type confounder NMI is 0.496 (global), with within-replicate NMI ranging from 0.379 to 0.745 (median: 0.592). The cell\\_subtype confounder NMI is 0.648 (global), with within-replicate NMI ranging from 0.224 to 0.679 (median: 0.636)."},{"key":"read_file:57b06f3debbf34b16b0a65b4aaf48a7b7eaf6c3118e1977ebf5d3b6768ba963e:84","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aec15262a02997f0","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T18:44:19.435Z","result":"{\n  \"question\": \"Are there distinct metabolic states within cell_subtype in ['CD8 T cells']?\",\n  \"analysis_scope\": {\n    \"field\": \"cell_subtype\",\n    \"values\": [\n      \"CD8 T cells\"\n    ],\n    \"source_cells_selected\": 3624\n  },\n  \"conclusion\": \"inconclusive\",\n  \"interpretation\": \"Metabolic-only cell-group separation is described by actual labels, seed stability, gene-set controls and within-replicate sensitivity. Th