is examined associations between metabolic clusters and cell types across all samples. The stratified cell-type associations show moderate NMI values, but the patient and sample confounders also contribute significantly to cluster composition.\n\n\\subsubsection{Cluster Composition}\nCluster sizes range from 714 to 8,806 cells. The composition analysis shows that clusters are associated with cell types but are not exclusively defined by them.\n\n\\subsubsection{Patient and Sample Effects}"},{"key":"read_file:3ebba2cf8ebaf7c9d84d1b1f0e74ce1a1be7ac6d390bfc4eed3921f3ad349c71:97","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-928faa7c3beafd45","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T19:12:38.059Z","result":"{\n  \"engine\": \"workflow_research_quality_metabolic_states_v2\",\n  \"engine_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\Desktop\\\\agentic\\\\workflow_codex\\\\tools\\\\research-quality\\\\metabolic_states.py\",\n  \"engine_sha256\": \"51ddbf26c336a932f10d216db6092bc5aa24f402adf9dafee6a0435382592401\",\n  \"methods\": {\n    \"unit\": \"Exact-symbol aggregated raw counts; all source features form each cell library-size denominator\",\n    \"normalization\": \"Per-cell library size to 10000, then log1p\",\n    \"feature_scaling\": \"Scanpy scale(zero_center=False, max_value=10)\",\n    \"pca\": {\n      \"solver\": \"arpack\",\n      \"zero_center\": true,\n      \"components\": 30,\n      \"seed\": 0\n    },\n    \"neighbors\": {\n      \"n_neighbors\": 15,\n      \"seed\": 0\n    },\n    \"leiden\": {\n      \"flavor\": \"igraph\",\n      \"n_iterations\": 2,\n      \"directed\": false\n    },\n    \"HVG_control\": \"Highest variance of library-normalized log1p expression among prevalence-passing non-mitochondrial symbols; no dispersion/mean bin normalization\",\n    \"random_controls\": \"Size-matched sampling without replacement from prevalence-passing no