yzed the Choudhury et al. 2022 meningioma study (3CA:20773), a 10x Genomics scRNA-seq dataset of 58,843 cells from 10 meningioma samples. The original study was published in \\textit{Nature Genetics} (DOI: 10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8) \\cite{choudhury2022}.\n\n\\subsection{Metabolic Gene Set}\nThe analysis used a user-supplied metabolic gene set from \\texttt{inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv}. This file contains 1,988 source gene symbols with mixed-case spelling. The analysis tool performed exact matching followed by case-insensitive matching, resulting in 1,646 matched genes for the global analysis and 1,318 matched genes for the CD8 T cell subset analysis.\n\n\\subsection{Normalization}\nCells were processed using the standard log-normalization method:\n\\begin{equation}\n    \\text{log\\_normalized} = \\log_2\\left(\\frac{\\text{UMI} + 1}{\\text{library\\_size}}\\right) \\times 10^4\n\\end{equation}"},{"key":"read_file:4e1cb5a4a9a869f3814812ade96f781c213b8cca6e30e7445875dd0abb304fc4:141","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-964fa453ab7f73ad","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:53:46.533Z","result":"\\begin{document}\n\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis report analyzes single-cell RNA-seq data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 meningioma study (3CA:20773) using user-supplied metabolic genes. We address three questions: (1) whether metabolic genes reveal reproducible transcriptional metabolic groupings across all cells, (2) the relationship between these groupings and known cell types/subtypes, and (3) whether distinct metabolic groupings exist within the CD8 T cell subtype.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Data and Methods}\n\n\\subsection{Dataset}"},{"key":"write_file:ae1249554fb5250c9e481d6ac3234a11fa91103ff2bca5b486a6d167d4f4f727","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-beaf3fb7f59471d5","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_cod