ncluded that results are \\textbf{inconclusive} for defining discrete biological metabolic states.\n\nThe silhouette score (0.217) is positive but weak. The HVG-based silhouette (0.283) exceeds the metabolic gene-based silhouette, indicating that highly variable genes capture more structure than the supplied metabolic genes. The random control comparison shows that 2 of 19 random gene controls exceeded or equal the metabolic gene clustering silhouette, with an add-one rank fraction of 0.15. This is a descriptive benchmark, not a biological P value.\n\nCluster sizes range from 714 to 8,806 cells. The resolution selection used a stability filter of mean pairwise ARI $\\ge$ 0.75, with stable candidates at resolutions 0.4, 0.8, and 1.2. The primary criterion was highest median silhouette across seeds, with tie-breaking by highest mean pairwise ARI.\n\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/core_analysis/metabolic_umap.pdf}\n    \\caption{Global metabolic gene clustering UMAP. Panel (a) shows 17 clusters identified using 1,646 matched metabolic genes across 58,843 cells. Panel (b) displays cluster size distribution. Panel (c) presents silhouette scores across resolutions.}\n    \\label{fig:global_umap}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/core_analysis/clustering_diagnostics.pdf}"},{"key":"read_file:563b4aa99d1b3bc5d6781b0398c5b59c09192a750227db8124b1e459c785e78c:156","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-973fbd741085daee","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T21:35:24.345Z","result":""},{"key":"read_file:71136d0d4da29ad48ebb2407692024dfc68ea66921f0e125434d904ea10a78f8:156","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad656311545d63b2","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T21:35:03.476Z","result":"ERROR: ENOENT: no such file or directory, lstat 'C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\3CA\\QA_R4\\figures\\core_analysis'"},{"key":"read_file:c4362f9b639ff7c15e05620e37e825757bce31800161f96a7a022dae4b48ce08:156","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcf105c0e8a99b07","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T21:35:33.182Z","result":"\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/core_analysis/metabolic_umap.pdf}\n    \\caption{Global metabolic gene clustering UMAP. Panel (a) shows 17 clusters identified using 1,646 matched metabolic genes across 58,843 cells. Panel (b) displays cluster size distribution. Panel (c) presents silhouette scores across resolutions.}\n    \\label{fig:global_umap}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/core_analysis/clustering_diagnostics.pdf}\n    \\caption{Global clustering diagnostics. Panel (a) shows cluster size distribution (n=17 clusters). Panel (b) displays cell-type association metrics. Panel (c) presents patient/sample confounder NMI values.}\n    \\label{fig:global_diagnostics}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\caption{Global clustering metrics and resolution selection.}\n    \\label{tab:global_metrics}\n    \\begin{tabular}{llr}\n        \\toprule\n        \\textbf{Metric} & \\textbf{Value} & \\textbf{Unit} \\\\\n        \\midrule\n        Cells analyzed & 58,843 & cells \\\\\n        Metabolic genes analyzed & 1,646 & genes \\\\\n        Clusters identified & 17 & \\\\\n        Silhouette score & 0.217 & \\\\\n        Resolution selection criterion & Median silhouette & \\\\\n        Random controls total & 19 & \\\\\n        Random controls exceeding observed & 2 & \\\\\n        Add-one rank fraction & 0.15 & \\\\\n        \\bottomrule\n    \\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n\nThe categorical confounder NMI values show that clustering is strongly associated with cell subtype (NMI = 0.648) and moderately associated with cell type (NMI = 0.496). Patient confounder NMI is 0.518, indicating that clustering is also driven by patient structure. Within-replicate analysis across 6 patients shows global-vs-within ARI ranging from 0.071 to 0.676, with patient 3 being the weakest replicate (3,287 cells).\n\n\\subsection{Question 2: Relationship Between Metabolic Groupings and Cell Types}\n\nThe clustering shows moderate association with cell type (global NMI = 0.496) and stronger association with cell subtype (global NMI = 0.648). This indicates that the metabolic gene-based clustering is partially driven by cell type identity rather than independent metabolic programs.\n\nWithin each biological replicate (patient), clustering is driven by patient/sample structure. The within-replicate ARI range (0.071 to 0.676) suggests that clusters are not consistently reproducible across patients. The weakest replicate (patient 3) has only 3,287 cells, limiting statistical power.\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\caption{Cell type association and confounder metrics for global analysis.}\n    \\label{tab:confounders}\n    \\begin{tabular}{llr}\n        \\toprule\n        \\textbf{Confounder} & \\textbf{Global NMI} & \\textbf{Within-replicate NMI (min-max)} \\\\\n        \\midrule"},{"key":"read_file:ace4fac137e0fc91f7c1d4b03c5efb8ae95e19f3484b849712cc918dce9edbaa:156","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b551527a75665bfb","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T21:34:47.266Z","result":"{\n  \"engine\": \"workflow_research_quality_metabolic_states_v2\",\n  \"engine_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\Desktop\\\\agentic\\\\workflow_codex\\\\tools\\\