onclusive} for defining discrete biological metabolic states.\n\nThe silhouette score (0.217) is positive but weak. The HVG-based silhouette (0.283) exceeds the metabolic gene-based silhouette, indicating that highly variable genes capture more structure than the supplied metabolic genes. The random control comparison shows that 2 of 19 random gene controls exceeded or equal the metabolic gene clustering silhouette, with an add-one rank fraction of 0.15. This is a descriptive benchmark, not a biological P value.\n\nCluster sizes range from 714 to 8,806 cells. The resolution selection used a stability filter of mean pairwise ARI $\\ge$ 0.75, with stable candidates at resolutions 0.4, 0.8, and 1.2. The primary criterion was highest median silhouette across seeds, with tie-breaking by highest mean pairwise ARI.\n\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/core_analysis/metabolic_umap.pdf}\n    \\caption{Global metabolic gene clustering UMAP. Panel (a) shows 17 clusters identified using 1,646 matched metabolic genes across 58,843 cells. Panel (b) displays cluster size distribution. Panel (c) presents silhouette scores across resolutions.}\n    \\label{fig:global_umap}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/core_analysis/clustering_diagnostics.pdf}"},{"key":"read_file:74c64ff2392719cebb6d001bf4c131676cee2abe1992cdfbcc67310c9e044573:156","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae8c2e1ab46654d4","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T21:36:00.116Z","result":"{\n  \"engine\": \"workflow_research_quality_metabolic_states_v2\",\n  \"engine_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\Desktop\\\\agentic\\\\workflow_codex\\\\tools\\\\research-quality\\\\metabolic_states.py\",\n  \"engine_sha256\": \"51ddbf26c336a932f10d216db6092bc5aa24f402adf9dafee6a043538259