seeds\",\n      \"tie_breaker\": \"highest mean_pairwise_ari\",\n      \"selected_resolution\": 0.8\n    },\n    \"cluster_size_summary\": {\n      \"minimum_cells\": 714,\n      \"minimum_cluster\": \"13\",\n      \"maximum_cells\": 8806,\n      \"maximum_cluster\": \"14\"\n    },\n    \"metrics\": {\n      \"silhouette\": 0.21661581099033356,"},{"key":"read_file:4b1650257c0190d200628125498885db9ac1f6ad7f3a94882425eea9e69ca507:156","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac9c037f1356a7b5","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T21:36:11.877Z","result":"Using the user-supplied metabolic genes across all 58,843 cells, we identified 17 clusters at resolution 0.8. The analysis concluded that results are \\textbf{inconclusive} for defining discrete biological metabolic states.\n\nThe silhouette score (0.217) is positive but weak. The HVG-based silhouette (0.283) exceeds the metabolic gene-based silhouette, indicating that highly variable genes capture more structure than the supplied metabolic genes. The random control comparison shows that 2 of 19 random gene controls exceeded or equal the metabolic gene clustering silhouette, with an add-one rank fraction of 0.15. This is a descriptive benchmark, not a biological P value.\n\nCluster sizes range from 714 to 8,806 cells. The resolution selection used a stability filter of mean pairwise ARI $\\ge$ 0.75, with stable candidates at resolutions 0.4, 0.8, and 1.2. The primary criterion was highest median silhouette across seeds, with tie-breaking by highest mean pairwise ARI.\n\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/core_analysis/metabolic_umap.pdf}\n    \\caption{Global metabolic gene clustering UMAP. Panel (a) shows 17 clusters identified using 1,646 matched metabolic genes across 58,843 cells. Panel (b) displays cluster size distribution. Panel (c) presents silhouette scores across resolutions.}\n    \\label{fig:global_umap}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/core_analysis/clustering_diagnostics.pdf}\n    \\caption{Global clustering diagnostics. Panel (a) shows cluster size distribution (n=17 clusters). Panel (b) displays cell-type association metrics. Panel (c) presents patient/sample confounder NMI values.}\n    \\label{fig:global_diagnostics}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\caption{Global clustering metrics and resolution selection.}\n    \\label{tab:global_metrics}\n    \\begin{tabular}{llr}\n        \\toprule\n        \\textbf{Metric} & \\textbf{Value} & \\textbf{Unit} \\\\\n        \\midrule\n        Cells analyzed & 58,843 & cells \\\\\n        Metabolic genes analyzed & 1,646 & genes \\\\\n        Clusters identified & 17 & \\\\\n        Silhouette score & 0.217 & \\\\\n        Resolution selection criterion & Median silhouette & \\\\\n        Random controls total & 19 & \\\\\n        Random controls exceeding observed & 2 & \\\\\n        Add-one rank fraction & 0.15 & \\\\"},{"key":"read_file:5d9626d477f61daa6ba24f649708ec7608df14ba5e155009fcc5e17390c52157:156","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a46790502f28da48","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T21:36:30.003Z","result":"{\n  \"question\": \"Are there distinct clusters of transcriptional metabolic states?\",\n  \"analysis_scope\": {\n    \"field\": null,\n    \"values\": [],\n    \"source_cells_selected\": 58843\n  },\n  \"conclusion\": \"inconclusive\",\n  \"interpretation\": \"Metabolic-only cell-group separation is described by actual labels, seed stability, gene-set controls and within-replicate sensitivity. These exploratory results do not by themselves establish discrete biological metabolic states or their absence.\",\