these groupings and known cell types/subtypes, and (3) whether distinct metabolic groupings exist within CD8 T cells specifically.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Data and Methods}"},{"key":"write_file:5039f45804becc11a7aebabc2b97de06e0be4240c386aa8045069445c5255598","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-879c35bb0b6c904d","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:16:00.198Z","result":"Wrote 8483 bytes to report\\main.tex"},{"key":"read_file:6b9c3f38ea4f6dce75dc3448941bd3bf100f2dde509ba1c42def997b6aa11816:174","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bcf3e7a89e8e216","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:26:13.081Z","result":"\\subsection{Clustering}\nClustering was performed using Scanpy's Leiden algorithm with resolution selection based on silhouette score and ARI stability. Random gene controls (19 draws) were used for baseline comparison.\n\n\\section{Results}\n\n\\subsection{Question 1: Reproducible Metabolic Groupings Across All Cells}\n\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=0.8\\textwidth]{figures/metabolic_umap.pdf}\n    \\caption{UMAP visualization of global metabolic clustering across all 58,843 cells using 1,646 metabolic genes. Cells are colored by Leiden cluster (17 clusters). This panel shows the global metabolic grouping structure.}\n    \\label{fig:global_umap}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering"},{"key":"read_file:8b60245ecb5a1a027c3c068c5c7a22ff8eda374d478c40c6ce3e74c25731f2af:174","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94364a563bca6d08","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:26:16.750Z","result":"\\date{\\today}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis report analyzes single-cell RNA-seq data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 meningioma study (3CA:20773) using a user-supplied set of metabolic genes. We address three questions: (1) whether metabolic genes reveal reproducible transcriptional metabolic groupings across all cells, (2) the relationship between these groupings and known cell types/subtypes, and (3) whether distinct metabolic groupings exist within CD8 T cells specifically.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Data and Methods}\n\n\\subsection{Data Source}\nThe analysis uses raw UMI-count data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 study (3CA:20773), a 10x Genomics scRNA-seq dataset of 58,843 cells from 10 meningioma samples. The study was published in \\textit{Nature Genetics} (DOI: 10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8) \\cite{choudhury2022}.\n\n\\subsection{Metabolic Gene Set}"},{"key":"read_file:c1981d4403dd5aab2d62edcf99e55bb1903ed6f2f88343292b3081a411c61c46:174","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-952d7b2f8dbeaa8b","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:26:19.810Z","result":"\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{amsmath}\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\n\\title{Single-Cell Metabolic State Analysis Using Choudhury et al. 2022 Data}\n\\author{QA_R4 Research Analysis}\n\\date{\\today}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis report analyzes single-cell RNA-seq data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 meningioma study (3CA:20773) using a user-supplied set of metabolic genes. We address three questions: (1) whether metabolic genes reveal reproducible transcriptional metabolic groupings across all cells, (2) the relationship between these groupings and known cell types/subtypes, and (3) whether distinct metabolic groupings exist within CD8 T cells specifically.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Data and Methods}\n\n\\subsection{Data Source}\nThe analysis uses raw UMI-count data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 study (3CA:20773), a 10x Genomics scRNA-seq dataset of 58,843 cells from 10 meningioma samples. The study was published in \\textit{Nature Genetics} (DOI: 10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8) \\cite{choudhury2022}.\n\n\\subsection{Metabolic Gene Set}\nA user-supplied gene set \\texttt{inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv} containing 1,988 gene symbols was used. After matching to the expression matrix, 1,646 unique genes were retained for the global analysis.\n\n\\subsection{Normalization}\nCells were filtered for QC metrics, then log-normalized using the following formula:\n\\begin{equation}"},{"key":"read_file:c82c2a64e8ecb7d764787e26f98a0a2de492ebc3c1ab116c2c958f0843b5d34a:174","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bef36eeadb49cd41","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:26:23.417Z","result":"\\subsection{Metabolic Gene Set}\nA user-supplied gene set \\texttt{inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv} containing 1,988 gene symbols was used. After matching to the expression matrix, 1,646 unique genes were retained for the global analysis.\n\n\\subsection{Normalization}\nCells were filtered for QC metrics, then log-normalized using the following formula:\n\\begin{equation}\n    \\text{log-normalized expression} = \\log_2\\left(\\frac{\\text{UMI count} + 1}{\\text{library size}}\\right)\n\\end{equation}\nwhere $\\text{UMI count}$ is the raw UMI count for a gene in a cell, and $\\text{library size}$ is the total UMI count per cell.\n\n\\subsection{Clustering}\nClustering was performed using Scanpy's Leiden algorithm with resolution selection based on silhouette score and ARI stability. Random gene controls (19 draws) were used for baseline comparison.\n\n\\section{Results}\n\n\\subsection{Question 1: Reproducible Metabolic Groupings Across All Cells}\n\n\\begin{figure}[h]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=0.8\\textwidth]{figures/metabolic_umap.pdf}\n    \\caption{UMAP visualization of global metabolic clustering across all 58,843 cells using 1,646 metabolic genes. Cells are colored by Leiden cluster (17 clusters). This panel shows the global metabolic grouping structure.}"},{"key":"read_file:de721c5173e9547d4f1046840f7d9500057556734c63b91af9688ca8f467de05:174","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaae83c8100a8198","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:26:27.048Z","result":"\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis report analyzes single-cell RNA-seq data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 meningioma study (3CA:20773) using a user-supplied set of metabolic genes. We address three questions: (1) whether metabolic genes reveal reproducible transcriptional metabolic groupings across all cells, (2) the relationship between these groupings and known cell types/subtypes, and (3) whether distinct metabolic groupings exist within CD8 T cells specifically.\n\\end{abstract}"},{"key":"read_file:b488e7c230ede8efc5e5c1ee15b97b8148535c7b66c718355acee734a12a16a2:174","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86274a482624b30a","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:26:30.071Z","result":"\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis report analyzes single-cell RNA-seq data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 meningioma study (3CA:20773) using a user-supplied set of metabolic genes. We address three questions: (1) whether metabolic genes reveal reproducible transcriptional metabolic groupings across all cells, (2) the relationship between these groupings and known cell types/subtypes, and (3) whether distinct metabolic groupings exist within 