2:58:29.134Z","result":"\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{amsmath}\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\n\\title{Single-Cell Metabolic State Analysis Using Choudhury et al. 2022 Data}\n\\author{QA\\_R4 Research Analysis}\n\\date{\\today}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis report analyzes single-cell RNA-seq data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 meningioma study (3CA:20773) using a user-supplied set of metabolic genes. We address three questions: (1) whether metabolic genes reveal reproducible transcriptional metabolic groupings across all cells, (2) the relationship between these groupings and known cell types/subtypes, and (3) whether distinct metabolic groupings exist within CD8 T cells specifically.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Data and Methods}\n\n\\subsection{Data Source}\nThe analysis uses raw UMI-count data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 study (3CA:20773), a 10x Genomics scRNA-seq dataset of 58,843 cells from 10 meningioma samples. The study was published in \\textit{Nature Genetics} (DOI: 10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8).\n\n\\subsection{Metabolic Gene Set}\nA user-supplied gene set $\\texttt{inputs/metabolic\\_genes\\_total.csv}$ containing 1,988 gene symbols was used. After matching to the expression matrix, 1,646 unique genes were retained for the global analysis.\n\n\\subsection{Normalization}\nCells were filtered for QC metrics, then log-normalized using the following formula:\n\\begin{equation}\n    \\text{log1p}(X_{ij}) = \\log(X_{ij} + 1)\n\\end{equation}\nwhere $X_{ij}$ is the UMI count for gene $i$ in cell $j$, and $\\log$ denotes the natural logarithm.\n\n\\section{Results}\n\n\\subsection{Question 1: Reproducible Metabolic Groupings Across All Cells}\nThe global analysis of 58,843 cells using 1,646 metabolic genes yielded 17 clusters at the selected resolution. Clustering diagnostics showed a mean pairwise ARI of 0.8 across controls. The metabolic UMAP (Figure \\ref{fig:global_umap}) displays the distribution of cells across metabolic clusters, with color representing cluster assignment.\n\n\\begin{figure}[htbp]\n    \\centering\n    \\includegraphics[width=0.8\\textwidth]{figures/metabolic_umap.pdf}\n    \\caption{Global metabolic UMAP showing 17 clusters across 58,843 cells. Each point represents a cell colored by its metabolic cluster assignment.}\n    \\label{fig:global_umap}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\begin{table}[htbp]\n    \\centering\n    \\caption{Cluster size summary for global analysis}\n    \\label{tab:cluster_sizes}"},{"key":"read_file:d2018f66d6425c03354720060dbbaa95c9473991509541e1b930768e879f448d:186","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa42ff2cf8e88468","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:58:38.937Z","result":"{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"dataset\": {\n    \"study_id\": \"3ca:20773\",\n    \"source_url\": \"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/4y8x28n9v6y5bkss3mqgu/Data_Choudhury2022_Brain.tar.gz?rlkey=3jhc85s8p3tp5jatdrauh6ka7&dl=1\",\n    \"sha256\": \"2156a73fd5f95a198ef90821f2d734bfa7e0b5aa3686deefd1b5c5d5d1269aa1\",\n    \"expression_path\": \"inputs/Exp_data_UMIcounts.mtx\",\n    \"cells_path\": \"inputs/Cells.csv\",\n    \"gene_names_path\": \"inputs/Genes.txt\",\n    \"n_cells\": 58843,\n    \"n_genes\": 33538,\n    \"matrix_orientation\": \"genes_by_cells\",\n    \"cell_id_column\": \"cell_name\"\n  },\n  \"feature_set\": {\n    \"name\": \"User-supplied metabolic genes\",\n    \"source_url\": \"local-user-supplied-input\",\n    \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-13T15:15:45.001Z\",\n    \"sha256\": \"7503180d29693bd1e654ea93281db0e3ec4177ff44842c8b02f6a098402e41a9\",\n    \"genes_path\": \"inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv\",\n    \"matched_genes_path\": \"results/core_analysis/matched_metabolic_genes.txt\",\n    \"source_gene_count\": 1988,\n    \"matched_gene_count\": 1646\n  },\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"engine\": \"workflow_research_quality_metabolic_states_v2\",\n    \"core_result_path\": \"results/core_analysis/core_result.json\",\n    \"core_result_sha256\": \"0da19b546073463f6341cb411b21287f3e50b2b9733a6f39dfc53e1fb9ca5848\",\n    \"input_unit\": \"cell\",\n    \"rows_analyzed\": 58843,\n    \"unique_cells_analyzed\": 58843,\n    \"random_seeds\": [0],\n    \"baselines\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"HVG and random size-matched controls\",\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"random_controls_exceeding_or_equal\": 2,\n          \"random_controls_total\": 19,\n          \"add_one_rank_fraction\": 0.15\n        },\n        \"result_path\": \"results/core_analysis/baseline_metrics.csv\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"confounders_checked\": [\"patient\", \"cell_type\", \"sample\", \"source\", \"cell_subtype\", \"cell_cycle_phase\", \"complexity\", \"computed_total_counts\", \"computed_detected_genes\", \"computed_mito_percent\"],\n    \"methods\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Scanpy Leiden on supplied metabolic genes\",\n        \"labels_path\": \"results/core_analysis/cluster_labels.csv\",\n        \"cell_id_column\": \"cell_name\",\n        \"label_column\": \"cluster\",\n        \"n_clusters\": 17,\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"silhouette\": 0.21661581099033356,\n          \"mean_pairwise_ari\": 0.9650730581380069,\n          \"median_silhouette\": 0.22155894339084625\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"subgroup_analyses\": [\n      {\n        \"scope\": {\n          \"field\": \"cell_subtype\",\n          \"values\": [\"CD8 T cells\"]\n        },\n        \"core_result_path\": \"results/cd8_analysis/core_result.json\",\n        \"core_result_sha256\": \"50950f343600c9c0dd17ed5191a3511cc2fb397d1b026120f4fe47ca6ab1f102\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"references\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"choudhury_2022\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8\",\n      \"metadata_path\": \"sources/literature/crossref_db798362115f799a.json\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"artifacts\": {\n    \"tex\": \"report/main.tex\",\n    \"pdf\": \"report/main.pdf\",\n    \"summary\": \"results/summary.json\",\n    \"figures\": [\n      \"figures/metabolic_umap.pdf\",\n      \"figures/clustering_diagnostics.pdf\",\n      \"figures/cd8_analysis/metabolic_umap.pdf\",\n      \"figures/cd8_analysis/clustering_diagnostics.pdf\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n"},{"key":"read_file:7d6441497d2a000b8143602a7817c90abe7db88e139f89c062a1c36cfe0ad9d6:186","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82f43a4b7fafad29","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:58:44.314Z","result":"# Single-Cell Metabolic State Analysis (QA_R4)\n\n## Overview\n\nThis repository contains the analysis of single-cell RNA-seq data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 meningioma study (3CA:20773) using user-supplied metabolic genes to investigate transcriptional metabolic states.\n\n## Dataset\n\n- **Study**: Choudhury et al. 2022 - Meningioma DNA methylation groups identify biological drivers and therapeutic vulnerabilities\n- **3CA ID**: 3ca:20773\n- **DOI**: 10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8\n- **Platform**: 10x Genomics\n- **Samples**: 10\n- **Cells**: 58,843\n- **Genes**: 33,538 (33,514 unique symbols, 24 duplicate symbol rows aggregated)\n\n## Analysis\n\n### User-Supplied Metabolic Genes\n\nThe analysis used a user-supplied gene set from `inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv`:\n- **Source gene symbols**: 1,988\n- **Global analysis matched genes**: 1,646\n- **CD8 T cell subset matched genes**: 1,318\n\n### Analysis Scope\n\n1. **Global Analysis**: All 58,843 cells using 1,646 metabolic genes\n   - Clusters identified: 17\n   - Conclusion: Inconclusive for discrete metabolic states\n\n2. **CD8 T Cell Subset Analysis**: 3,624 CD8 T cells using 1,318 metabolic genes\n   - Clusters identified: 6\n   - Conclusion: Inconclusive for discrete metabolic states\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Question 1: Reproducible Metabolic Groupings Across All Cells\n\nUsing the user-supplied metabolic genes across all 58,843 cells, the analysis identified 17 clusters. However, the results are **inconclusive** for defining discrete metabolic states. The clustering is primarily driven by cell type identity and patient/sample structure rather than independent metabolic programs.\n\n### Question 2: Relationship Between Groupings and Cell Types\n\nThe clustering shows strong association with cell type and cell subtype metadata:\n- **Cell type NMI**: 0.496 (global)\n- **Cell subtype NMI**: 0.648 (global)\n- **Patient NMI**: 0.518\n- **Sample NMI**: 0.548\n\nThis indicates that the observed clustering is largely explained by known biological and technical confounders.\n\n### Question 3: Metabolic Groupings Within CD8 T Cells\n\nWithin the CD8 T cell subtype (n=3,624), the analysis identified 6 clusters using 1,318 metabolic genes. The results are also **inconclusive** for defining discrete metabolic states. The clustering is driven by patient/sample structure rather than independent metabolic subtypes.\n\n## Limitations\n\n1. **Descriptive Metrics Only**: Cell-level clustering metrics (silhouette, ARI, NMI) are descriptive and do not constitute statistical significance tests.\n\n2. **No Discrete State Proof**: The analysis does not establish discrete biological metabolic states; it only describes observed separation patterns.\n\n3. **Confounder Influence**: Patient and sample confounders strongly influence clustering, limiting biological interpretation.\n\n4. **Not Independent Validation**: Clusters derived from the same expression matrix cannot be used for independent hypothesis testing.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- `report/main.tex`: LaTeX source document\n- `report/main.pdf`: Compiled PDF report\n- `results/summary.json`: Global analysis summary\n- `results/cd8_analysis/summary.json`: CD8 T cell subset analysis summary\n- `results/core_analysis/core_result.json`: Global core analysis results\n- `results/cd8_analysis/core_result.json`: CD8 T cell core analysis results\n- `results/analysis_manifest.json`: Analysis manifest with metadata\n- `figures/clustering_diagnostics.pdf`: Global clustering diagnostics\n- `figures/cd8_analysis/clustering_diagnostics.pdf`: CD8 T cell clustering diagnostics\n\n## References\n\n1. Choudhury, A., Magill, S. T., Eaton, C. D., et al. (2022). Meningioma DNA methylation groups identify biological drivers and therapeutic vulnerabilities. *Nature Genetics*, 54(5), 649-659. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8\n\n2. Stuart, A. J., Butler, A., Hoffman, P., et al. (2019). Comprehensive integration of single-cell data. *Cell*, 177(7), 1888-1902. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2019.05.031\n"},{"key":"write_file:b89f658d5e28c75c2c0ac98c23f586269039e9b47e56b9e5c6448fc8e038236a","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a59638bbc9c82234","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T15:56:19.827Z","result":"Wrote 39 bytes to figures\\check_files.txt"},{"key":"read_file:8a1ca57355d06f1f2e044f2d95c11d3ceb05fa012b96f45bc3e71e0155408a14:186","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92319d6f73bfa3bb","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:59:11.751Z","result":"Checking figures directory contents...\nThis file will be used to verify what files exist in the figures directory.\n"},{"key":"read_file:ace4fac137e0fc91f7c1d4b03c5efb8ae95e19f3484b849712cc918dce9edbaa:186","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8456281407c9816b","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T22:58:17.182Z","result":"{\n  \"engine\": \"workflow_research_quality_metabol