s\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T23:17:59.541Z","result":"\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{amsmath}\n\\usepackage{amssymb}\n\\usepackage{geometry}\n\\geometry{margin=1in}\n\n\\title{\\textbf{Single-Cell Metabolic State Analysis Using User-Supplied Metabolic Genes}}\n\\author{QA_R4 Research Analysis}\n\\date{\\today}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis report analyzes single-cell RNA-seq data from the Choudhury et al. 2022 meningioma study (3CA:20773) using a user-supplied set of metabolic genes. We address three questions: (1) whether global metabolic grouping is reproducible across all cells, (2) the relationship between metabolic clusters and known cell types, and (3) whether distinct metabolic states exist within CD8 T cells. Results are described as inconclusive for discrete metabolic states, with confounding by cell type and patient/sample effects observed.\n\\end{abstract}"},{"key":"replace_in_file:aed9f5d47fb438e05e462b64a5f94b452682c298505ca8336426d4acf971d00f","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bc2e7119bbe3db7","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T23:18:24.753Z","result":"Replaced one block in report\\main.tex"},{"key":"build_research_report:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a:195","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0738bb25ef63787","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T23:20:05.860Z","result":"ERROR: {\"error\": \"pdflatex pass 1 failed with exit code 1:\\nThis is pdfTeX, Version 3.141592653-2.6-1.40.29 (MiKTeX 26.5) (preload