26\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T23:20:21.910Z","result":"\nUser-supplied metabolic genes were provided in \\texttt{inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv} with 1,988 source gene symbols. After matching to expression features, 1,646 genes were retained for global analysis and 1,318 genes for CD8 T cell analysis.\n\n\\subsection{Normalization}\nCells were filtered for QC metrics (mitochondrial fraction, library size). Expression values were log-normalized as follows:\n\\begin{equation}\n    \\text{log\\_normalized} = \\log_2(\\text{UMI} + 1) - \\log_2(\\text{median library size})\n\\end{equation}\nwhere \\texttt{UMI} is the unique molecular identifier count and \\texttt{median library size} is the median UMI count across cells.\n\n\\subsection{Clustering}\nClustering was performed using Leiden algorithm with resolution parameters selected to maximize silhouette coefficient. Random gene controls (19 draws) were used to establish baseline performance.\n\n\\section{Results}\n\n\\subsection{Question 1: Global Metabolic Grouping Reproducibility}"},{"key":"read_file:4bf0710a249a2b81b7f8f31895f0268a0ab4363e4ddc5819bf41f2ddd41035a5:195","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4fe2d1dc3379f97","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T23:20:26.770Z","result":"\\subsection{Data Sources}\nThe expression matrix originates from the Choudhury et al. 2022 study (DOI: 10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8), available via the Curated Cancer Cell Atlas (3CA:20773). The study contains 58,843 cells from 10 meningioma samples sequenced on 10x Genomics technology.\n\nUser-supplied metabolic genes were provided in \\texttt{inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv} with 1,988 source gene symbols. After matching to expression features, 1,646 genes were retained for global analysis and 1,318 genes for CD8 T cell analysis.\n\n\\subsection{Normalization}\nCells were filtered for QC metrics (mitochondrial fraction, library size). Expression values were log-normalized as follows:\n\\begin{equation}"},{"key":"read_file:86b67ff5a2577a11f4e7887b070276097d3893271469b9aa2698fe5e1f00e3e3:195","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a7c3c7ad8801a1c","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T23:20:33.218Z","result":"\\subsection{Data Sources}\nThe expression matrix originates from the Choudhury et al. 2022 study (DOI: 10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8), available via the Curated Cancer Cell Atlas (3CA:20773). The study contains 58,843 cells from 10 meningioma samples sequenced on 10x Genomics technology.\n\nUser-supplied metabolic genes were provided in \\texttt{inputs/metabolic_genes_total.csv} with 1,988 source gene symbols. After matching to expression features, 1,646 genes were retained for global analysis and 1,318 genes for CD8 T cell analysis.\n\n\\subsection{Normalization}\nCells were filtered for QC metrics (mitochondrial fraction, library size). Expression values were log-normalized as follows:\n\\begin{equation}\n    \\text{log\\_normalized} = \\log_2(\\text{UMI} + 1) - \\log_2(\\text{median library size})\n\\end{equation}\nwhere \\texttt{UMI} is the unique molecular identifier count and \\texttt{median library size} is the median UMI count across cells.\n\n\\subsection{Clustering}"},{"key":"read_file:6b9c3f38ea4f6dce75dc3448941bd3bf100f2dde509ba1c42def997b6aa11816:195","call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a711728ad2c4eb5f","session":"C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\agentic\\workflow_codex\\.runtime\\codex-home\\sessions\\2026\\09\\13\\rollout-2026-09-13T23-08-39-0b785373-9b3.jsonl","timestamp":"2026-09-13T23:21:10.461Z","result":"\n\\section{Methods}\n\n\\subsection{Data Sources}\nThe expression matrix originates from the Choudhury et al. 2022 study (DOI: 10.1038/s41588-022-01061-8), available via the Curated